WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Speaker 1: Well, it happened yesterday just&nbsp;
after we were done filming our Thursday show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:12.240
Judge Tunji Brown Jackson has been confirmed by&nbsp;
the Senate 53 to 47. She will be the first black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.360
woman on the Supreme Court. It is a major deal and&nbsp;
I'm not going to spend a lot of time on it today&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.520
because we've basically spent the time already.&nbsp;
We've talked about her background. We've talked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.200
about her qualifications. We've talked about some&nbsp;
of the most disgusting confirmation hearings that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.680
we've seen. We've talked about Republicans saying&nbsp;
they're not going to vote for her without really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.920
being able to explain why they're not going&nbsp;
to vote for her. We've talked about all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:43.040
it and now she's been confirmed, and indeed it&nbsp;
was a 53 to 47 vote. It was the 48 Democrats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.240
the two independents that caucus with&nbsp;
Democrats and the three Republicans that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.600
we knew were going to support her because they&nbsp;
said so. And that was Senator Mitt Romney of Utah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.200
Senator Lisa Murkowski of Alaska and Senator Susan&nbsp;
Collins of Maine. No other Republican supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
one of, if not the most qualified Supreme&nbsp;
Court nominees in. As long as I've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.320
covering Supreme Court confirmation hearings&nbsp;
and when compared to the nine justices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:21.840
on the court up until now, as qualified as any of&nbsp;
them. So congratulations to her. We knew she'd be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:28.720
confirmed and now the next battle is going to&nbsp;
be. What happens if Joe Biden gets another pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.280
after the midterms and Republicans have taken&nbsp;
control of the Senate? Mitch McConnell was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:42.240
asked sometime in the last 24 hours if you guys&nbsp;
take the Senate in November. And Joe Biden gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.600
another pick. Would you even hold confirmation&nbsp;
hearings and Mitch McConnell declined to answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.480
And it's the same Partizan nonsense we've&nbsp;
been talking about for a long time. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:58.880
that's it for now. The right decision made Judge&nbsp;
Jackson will soon be Justice Jackson on the court.

